<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!--
      Lets the projects that target Windows be RESTORED on Linux.

      Five of ours are net10.0-windows -the server, the tests, the launcher, the
      deobfuscator and the Windows Forms contract- and that is fine: they run on Windows and that
      is where they run. What is not fine is that they cannot even be RESTORED elsewhere, because
      GitHub runs a job of its own over the repo -the dependency graph one, submit-nuget- that
      runs on Linux and restores the whole solution. Without this it stops at the first Windows
      project with NETSDK1100 and the check goes red even though nothing is broken.

      This does NOT build Windows Forms on Linux nor does it try to: it only allows resolving the
      framework references so as to be able to restore. Really building still wants Windows.
    -->
    <EnableWindowsTargeting>true</EnableWindowsTargeting>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
